IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-benefit-period`
IMPORT `ei1-caring`

-- Tests of ei1-caring.l4 (Act ss 23.1, 23.2 and 23.3(1) to (5)). Every expected value is written by hand from the
-- text of the section named beside the assertion; none is copied from the module's output. Dates were worked out with a
-- calendar program that is not the encoding. One #ASSERT per line.

§ `s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states a significant risk of death within 26 weeks (src:566-571, 588)`
-- args: the number of weeks within which the certificate says there is a significant risk of death; the shorter period prescribed, if any
#ASSERT `s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` 26 NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` 10 NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` 27 NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` 20 (JUST 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` 21 (JUST 20))

§ `s 23.1(3) a member of a prescribed class of practitioners (src:573)`
#ASSERT `s 23.1(3) the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(3) the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(3) the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` FALSE TRUE)

§ `s 23.1(2) benefits are payable for the care of a family member (src:566-571)`
-- args: major attachment claimant; a doctor or nurse practitioner issued a certificate; issued by a prescribed class under (3); the certificate states the risk of death within the period; the family member requires care or support
#ASSERT `s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 23.1(6) the exception to subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) (src:591-594)`
-- args: benefits already exhausted; the beginning of the period already determined; the filing would move it earlier; other circumstances in the regulations
#ASSERT `s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `ei1 the shape shared by s 23.1(4), s 23.2(3) and s 23.3(3) (src:575-583, 615-622, 651-659)`
-- args: a day in the week with which the period begins; the days of the events that end the period; the length in weeks
-- Wednesday 2026-03-11 is in the week of Sunday 2026-03-08; 52 weeks from it end on Saturday 2027-03-06.
#ASSERT (`ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) EMPTY 52)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 8
#ASSERT (`ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) EMPTY 52)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 6
-- an event on Wednesday 2026-06-17 ends it on Saturday 2026-06-20; the earliest of two events counts
#ASSERT (`ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17)) 52)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20
#ASSERT (`ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17), (YearMonthDay 2026 5 6)) 52)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 9
-- an event after the 52 weeks do not lengthen it
#ASSERT (`ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2027 6 17)) 52)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 6
-- a shorter period of 26 weeks ends on Saturday 2026-09-05
#ASSERT (`ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) EMPTY 26)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 9 5

§ `s 23.1(4) the period during which compassionate care benefits are payable (src:575-583, 589)`
-- args: the day the first certificate is issued and filed; the day from which the practitioner certifies (claim made first); the earlier day under 10(4) or (5);
-- (6) takes (4)(a)(ii) out; the day benefits are exhausted; the day the family member dies; the shorter period prescribed
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 8
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 6
-- the family member dies on Wednesday 2026-06-17
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17)) NOTHING)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 20
-- benefits exhausted on Wednesday 2026-05-06, before the death
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 6)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17)) NOTHING)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 9
-- the claim was made before the certificate was issued: the period begins with the week of the day the practitioner certifies from (Wednesday 2026-02-18, week of Sunday 2026-02-15)
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 18)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 15
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 18)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 2 13
-- subsection (6) takes (4)(a)(ii) out: back to the day of the certificate
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 18)) NOTHING TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 8
-- the claim is regarded as made on an earlier day (Sunday 2026-02-01): that day
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 1
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 1 30
-- a shorter period of 26 weeks is prescribed
#ASSERT (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (JUST 26))'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 9 5

§ `s 23.1(4.1) an additional certificate (src:585)`
#ASSERT `s 23.1(4.1) an additional certificate is needed for benefits payable after the end of the period of 26 weeks` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(4.1) an additional certificate is needed for benefits payable after the end of the period of 26 weeks` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 23.1(7) deferring the waiting period (src:596-599)`
-- args: the claimant makes a claim under section 23.1; (a) another has claimed and served or is serving; (b) another is claiming now and elects to serve; (c) prescribed requirements
#ASSERT `s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `s 23.1(8) to (10) dividing the weeks; a provincial allowance (src:601-607)`
#ASSERT `s 23.1(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 23.1(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` 13 13
#ASSERT `s 23.1(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` 26 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23.1(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` 14 13)
#ASSERT `s 23.1(9) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(9) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23.1(10) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` TRUE TRUE 400 150 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 23.1(10) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` TRUE TRUE 400 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23.1(10) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` TRUE FALSE 400 150 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 23.1(10) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` FALSE TRUE 400 150 EQUALS 400

§ `s 23.2(1) benefits for a critically ill child (src:609-614)`
-- args: major attachment claimant; a family member of a critically ill child; to care for that child; a practitioner issued a certificate; it states the child is critically ill and needs care; it sets out the period
